--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
WEB SOURCE SHAPE (read end-to-end — covenant #3)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
SqlPlaygroundPage.tsx is a manual, read-only SQL surface mounted at /power/sql. It owns NO API
data source (the manifest record id=page:power-user/SqlPlayground declares dataSources: none —
"renders from navigation values / local state"). Its render tree:
  - Page header: PageTitle(powerSql.title) + intro <p>(powerSql.intro)
  - <AINLSqlPlayground onApply={handleApplyAiDraft} />  (the opt-in Helix NL→SQL drafter; its own
    already-shipped P4 parity unit — TeslaSync/shared-surfaces/AINLSqlPlayground.* artifact 0035)
  - GlassPanel1 "Manual SQL editor": PanelTitle(powerSql.editor.title) + Textarea (placeholder
    powerSql.editor.placeholder, aria-label powerSql.editor.label, rows=10, spellCheck off) +
    Run(powerSql.editor.run)/Clear(powerSql.editor.clear) buttons disabled when the trimmed query
    is empty + a deterministic runMessage (powerSql.editor.runEmpty when blank | runUnavailable
    otherwise — the page exposes NO SQL execution endpoint; it instructs the user to copy into a
    read-only DB client)
  - GlassPanel2 "Curated schema catalog": PanelTitle(powerSql.catalog.title) + intro
    (powerSql.catalog.intro) + the name-sorted CURATED_CATALOG (5 install-static tables:
    drives / charging_sessions / vehicles / alerts / signal_log_view), each rendered with its name
    (mono cyan) + description and a 1-col/2-col responsive grid of columns (name mono green · type
    — description)
  - State persistence: the SQL textarea is persisted to localStorage under the canonical
    'ai.sqlPlayground.draft' key (survives navigate-away + back).
Faithful, non-narrowing parity (covenant #2/#5) therefore = reproduce the header + BOTH GlassPanels
(editor + catalog) AND host the real AINLSqlPlayground surface (DRY — no re-implementation), with
its onApply wired to copy a draft into the editor (web handleApplyAiDraft → setSql).

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
OUTPUT PATH RECONCILIATION (no silent drift — covenant #9)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
The generated prompt names the output dir `apps/apple/TeslaSync/Features/PowerUser/**`. That path
does NOT exist in this repo and is NOT a project.yml source group (the app targets list `Sources`
+ `TeslaSync/{widget-primitives,dashboard-widgets,feature-views,misc-surfaces,shared-surfaces}` —
there is no `TeslaSync/Features`). The repo's real, compiled canonical page home is
`apps/apple/Sources/Features/<Domain>/**` — where the sibling P7 pages ship (notifications/Webhooks,
notifications/AuditLog, admin/ApiPlayground, …) and which `Sources` already lists as a project.yml
source path (createIntermediateGroups). The page therefore ships at
`apps/apple/Sources/Features/PowerUser/**`, the faithful equivalent of the prompt's
`Features/PowerUser`; unit tests at `apps/apple/Tests/Unit/Features/PowerUser/**`. Strings ship in
the platform catalog `apps/apple/Localization/Localizable.xcstrings` (an allowed file). This is the
same reconciliation the sibling notifications-Webhooks / notifications-AuditLog logs recorded.

ROUTE HOSTING: the web route `/power/sql` is nested. A dedicated `.powerSql` AppRoute case is added
(pathSegment `power/sql` → `.path` `/power/sql` matching web exactly; System group alongside the
sibling power-user `.powerUser`; SF Symbol `tablecells` for the schema/SQL surface), `AppRouteParser`
aliases `/power/sql` → `.powerSql` (REQUIRED — the generic first-segment fallback splits on '/' and
would resolve the segment `power`, which matches no route, returning nil), and
`SqlPlaygroundRouteRegistration` hosts the page, chained into `\.routeHosts` in TeslaSyncApp.swift
right after `SystemRouteRegistration`. So the page is reachable via the System-group sidebar entry
and any `/power/sql` deep link. (Navigation registration is an allowed file per the prompt.)

