DISPOSITION
================================================================================
A complete, HIG-native SwiftUI SqlPlaygroundPage shipped at parity with the web source: a pure @Observable
SqlPlaygroundPageModel (ADR-004 — no networking in the view) exposing the page's 11 web i18n keys, the SQL editor
draft (persisted via an injectable SqlDraftStore — the web localStorage 'ai.sqlPlayground.draft' parity), the
Run/Clear/run-message logic, the name-sorted 5-table curated schema catalog, and a lazily-cached NLSqlPlaygroundModel
whose onApply copies a Helix-proposed draft into the editor (web handleApplyAiDraft, propose-only). The view
reproduces every web region — the header (title + intro), the hosted already-shipped AINLSqlPlayground Helix drafter
(reused, not re-implemented — DRY — with all its states), and both GlassPanels (the manual SQL editor textarea +
Run/Clear + deterministic run message, and the curated catalog with an adaptive column grid). A dedicated `.powerSql`
route (pathSegment `power/sql`, System group) + parser alias + registration make it sidebar-reachable and `/power/sql`
deep-linkable, preserving every RouteTests invariant. Verified on BOTH idioms by isolated Swift 6 strict-concurrency
type-checks (macOS 0/0 + iOS 0/0, incl. previews) and the executed model + route harness (24/24). The full xcodebuild
scheme was NOT run — it is gated on the out-of-scope, P1-owned KMP `Shared.xcframework` Gradle staging (the app module
imports `Shared`; staging OOM-kills this shared host per the sibling logs), and triggering it would be irresponsible
on a shared runner; deferred to its owner / the P99 integration gate.

